values ('lesswrong-rationalist-community-blog', 'rss', 'https://www.lesswrong.com/feed.xml', 'LessWrong', 'Rationalist community blog', 'en', 'LessWrong is a community blog devoted to rationality and AI safety discussion. This is its main feed: member written posts on AI control and alignment research, existential risk debates, personal essays on decision making, and the occasional technical paper. Anyone can publish here, so posts vary widely in topic and are not limited to official announcements from any single organization.', 195.9, null, null, '["My Current Model of What Happened to Elon Musk","You Should Apply to Inkhaven","Pretraining data, not verifiability, is why LLMs are especially good at math (and coding)"]')
