values ('nvidia-developer-technical-blog', 'rss', 'https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/feed', 'NVIDIA', 'Developer technical blog', 'en', 'NVIDIA is the company behind CUDA and the GPUs widely used for AI computing. This is its technical blog for developers, data scientists and IT admins: tutorials and deep dives on CUDA and TensorRT, inference benchmarking tools, model architecture comparisons such as dense versus mixture of experts designs, federated learning setups, and hardware topics like NVLink and edge deployment on Jetson. It is engineering and tooling content, not company press announcements.', 7.6, null, null, '["Benchmarking LLM Inference at Scale with AIPerf","How to Use AI Agents to Prepare 3D Scenes for Simulation","TensorRT Edge-LLM Completes the MLPerf Edge Agentic Benchmark 6.4x Faster on Jetson AGX Thor"]')
